Authenticates WAN interfaces against an IEEE 802.1X controlled port, as
required by some ISPs, campus and enterprise networks, before DHCP or
static addressing can work.

A wired wpa_supplicant runs on each configured interface (physical or
VLAN). Supported methods are PEAP and TTLS with MSCHAPv2 (TTLS also with
PAP), with optional server certificate and domain validation. The port is
re-authenticated when the link comes back up, and the current EAP state
and the last failure reason are shown in the GUI.
